ion to being  a sponsor of this conference Thank You  number kissed is also a nonprofit that  supports scientific open source projects  for scientific computing so they do this  by giving funds to projects that need  funds but also by giving infrastructure  and support for financial things and  legal things that if you're a very small  project you might not be equipped to  deal with so two Sigma became a gold  sponsor of Nome focus this year and  we're really excited to be working with  them so I'm gonna finish up my talk by  returning to this graph so  - Sigma does use open-source does  contribute open-source I would argue  that we are championing open-source but  what my job I think is is to try to  figure out how to get us into this blue  parts and we are still figuring out how  to do this but I hope that as this  community continues to be so kind and  helpful I can chat with all of you and  chat with a bunch of people and  hopefully not only to Sigma but a whole  bunch of companies can be here in the  future giving talks about how happy they  are to be in that upper right hand  corner so thank you guys so much for  viewing so nice this was really fun not  too scary um if you want to check out to  Sigma open-source projects there's two  Sigma I oh I've got my email address up  there I've got my website which I'll  warn you is all music but I still think  it's cool and I've got my Twitter handle  it's probably been three years since  I've treated but I could always get back  on the wagon um if you guys have any  questions I'd be happy to take them now  otherwise have a lovely lunch thank you  [Applause]  yeah  yeah that's interesting I hadn't thought  about that before the question was would  we ever be provided just open  information on exactly how our IP  steering committee and our approval  process works if other people want to  use that model yeah I'd be curious what  the Bloomberg model is we're we're  pretty transparent within the company  and that there's f